          "value": ""
        },
        "Speaker": {
          "type": "cexostring",
          "value": ""
        },
        "Text": {
          "type": "cexolocstring",
          "value": {
            "0": "*She digs in a pocket and comes up with a scrap of pale green glass, worn round at every edge, and holds it out on a flat palm.* This came off a window in Armenelos. It has been in the sea for an Age and in my pocket for ninety years and it has never once done anything.\n\nThat is why you are getting it. It is not a charm. It is a bill that has not been presented. Keep it on you, and go on with what you were doing, and one day the blood will cost you something -- a friend, a door shut in your face, a thing you did that you cannot put down. Everyone of our sort pays it. The ones who go bad are the ones who never noticed they had.\n\nWhen it costs you, come back and say out loud what it was."
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "__struct_id": 3,
        "Animation": {
          "type": "dword",
          "value": 0
        },
        "AnimLoop": {
          "type": "byte",
