        "Speaker": {
          "type": "cexostring",
          "value": ""
        },
        "Text": {
          "type": "cexolocstring",
          "value": {
            "0": "*She is up before you have finished crossing the grass, which she has never done, and she takes both your hands and turns them over and looks at them rather than at your face.* Say it.\n\nDo not tidy it up for me. I have heard four hundred years of tidied versions and they are worth nothing. Say the actual price, in the actual words, while you are still angry about it. That is the whole of the lesson, and it only works once."
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "__struct_id": 5,
        "Animation": {
          "type": "dword",
          "value": 0
        },
        "AnimLoop": {
          "type": "byte",
          "value": 1
