          "value": ""
        },
        "Text": {
          "type": "cexolocstring",
          "value": {
            "0": "*The woman at the fire nods you toward a dry piece of masonry.* Sit, warm yourself, it costs nothing. I am Erendis, and this heap of stones was the capital of the world once, which nobody believes until they are standing in it.\n\nNo, I do not tell fortunes. I sit with sorcerers. If you are not one, you are welcome to the fire and to the story of how Numenor went under, which is long and has no moral in it whatsoever."
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "__struct_id": 7,
        "Animation": {
          "type": "dword",
          "value": 0
        },
        "AnimLoop": {
          "type": "byte",
          "value": 1
