          "value": ""
        },
        "Text": {
          "type": "cexolocstring",
          "value": {
            "0": "*You say it. She does not comfort you, which is a mercy; she listens all the way to the end and then nods once, takes the glass out of your hand, and sets it into the head of a black lebethron staff she has evidently had ready for some time.*\n\nThat is the price paid and admitted. The staff is not lending you anything -- it is only that you have stopped arguing. Take it."
          }
        }
      }
